From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:55:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Drop only the init reference a failed
 init took

qmp_combo_com_init() takes a reference on init_count only for a normal
initialisation. A forced initialisation, which the Type-C orientation
and mode switches use to reprogram a PHY that is already in use, leaves
the count alone. The error path decrements init_count in both cases, so
a forced initialisation that fails, for example because a regulator or
clock cannot be enabled, drops a reference that belongs to one of the
PHY's users. The count then no longer matches the number of users, and
the common block is powered down on the wrong qmp_combo_com_exit() call
or not at all.

Decrement init_count on failure only when this call incremented it.

Fixes: 2851117f8f42 ("phy: qcom-qmp-combo: Introduce orientation switching")
Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index 45d0a805e30..912939cfbd8 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4402,7 +4402,8 @@ static int qmp_combo_com_init(struct qmp_combo *qmp, bool force)
 err_disable_regulators:
 	regulator_bulk_disable(cfg->num_vregs, qmp->vregs);
 err_decrement_count:
-	qmp->init_count--;
+	if (!force)
+		qmp->init_count--;
 
 	return ret;
 }
